+     * the allocation-info query, which passes no resource: it exists to size a
+     * heap for a placed resource, so it must answer exactly as the placed
+     * creation will or the heap comes out too small. The VKD3D_CONFIG overrides
+     * below deliberately still win over this.
+     *
+     * On this stack the cost of not doing it is total. disable_compression's only
+     * effect here is the branch below, which sets MUTABLE_FORMAT and then throws
+     * the format compatibility list away. Turnip does not implement
+     * VK_EXT_image_compression_control, so d3d12_device_should_use_image_compression_control
+     * is false and that side effect is the whole of what happens -- and Turnip's
+     * format_list_ubwc_possible fails closed on precisely that shape
